  "scope": "Failed Windows HDF5 writes preserve prior target; failed official FlyVis observations preserve last successful published state. No changes to geometry defaults, model weights, data or scientific protocols.",
  "excluded": "All preexisting untracked source, B1/B2/history source patches, learned-head followups, plan/catalogue/Obsidian, weights, datasets and experiment caches. Frozen source copies are local test input only, not additional publication payload.",
  "included_npz": "Only bounded synthetic/native observation replay inputs and outputs; no dataset or model cache.",
  "verification": "Shared tree and HEAD archive with only this overlay both passed. Full source hashes and commands are in validation.json.",
  "limits": "Separate native review probes explicitly used CPU without CUDA. The first shared package attempt accidentally included an existing native integration test with device=None; its actual device was not recorded, so CUDA use cannot be excluded. That test failed in the isolated archive because the vendor runtime was absent; initial logs are retained. It is explicitly deselected in both final package runs, with native coverage supplied by the independent CPU probes. Observation staging covers the official functional state update, not arbitrary in-place custom callbacks or external side effects. HDF5 tests require bundled h5py and skip when absent in the isolated archive. Two real symlink tests skip without Windows symlink privilege; a mocked target-resolution contract passes. Atomic replacement does not promise power-loss durability or multi-writer transactions. Hardlinked targets are rejected; actual 992-file HDF5 inventory contains no such aliases."
}